First, let's find an expression for $\dfrac{d}{dx}[4g(x)+h(x)-8]$ in terms of $g'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{d}{dx}[4g(x)+h(x)-8]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[4g(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}[h(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}(8)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=4g'(x)+h'(x)-0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $\dfrac{d}{dx}[4g(x)+h(x)-8]=4g'(x)+h'(x)$.
